    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/ha/adapter.py",
    "line": 220,
    "summary": "`read()` raises when no readings came back, not when every type's read failed, so one type's failure fails the whole read even though another type answered.",
    "failure_scenario": "On Virtual, the PIN read answers but every PIN slot is left out as silent (written too recently, still inside `read_lag`, or answered as cannot-tell), so it contributes `{}`. The password read raises NO_ANSWER. `failed and not readings` is true, so the password's error is raised for the whole read. The worker counts the lock as not answering and may back off, which contradicts the docstring ('the read fails only when every type's does'). The fix is to track which types succeeded rather than testing `not readings`."
