    "failure_scenario": "On Virtual this is cheap. Once Z-Wave or Matter (native users) write passwords, every poll, allocation pass and read-back doubles the lock traffic and spends the per-exchange budget twice. On slow or meshy locks (#1397) that doubles timeout exposure. A single `async_get_users(slots)` per read, projected per type, would avoid it."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/binary_sensor.py",
    "line": 65,
    "summary": "`managed_credential_types` depends on capabilities that are probed lazily, but it is sampled once when entities are created and once at hold time, so per-type sensors and tracked addresses can go stale.",
